From: premohq <48417750+premohq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:33:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS5-ECAM's Switch side: frame generation, its method and the
 speed limit for the game it starts

PS5-ECAM's launcher has this program's Frame generation (with MihawkGen) and Speed limit on its
Switch side, for the side and for each game, and starts a game with them as --set frame_gen,
frame_gen_method and speed_limit. They go over Settings and the game's own for that session as the
other --set settings do: PreferencesFor for frame generation, PerformanceFor (LoadPerformance's,
with the session's speed limit) for the speed limit. tools/check-performance-settings.py looks for
the session's PerformanceFor where it looked for LoadPerformance.
---
 headless/main.cpp                   |  5 +++--
 headless/settings_store.h           | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 tools/check-performance-settings.py |  8 ++++++--
 3 files changed, 31 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/headless/main.cpp b/headless/main.cpp
index 67475bb..db0819e 100644
--- a/headless/main.cpp
+++ b/headless/main.cpp
@@ -1320,8 +1320,9 @@ int main(int argc, char** argv) {
                                     " Hz, ASTC textures " + (astc_full ? "decoded" : "as BC3")).c_str());
             // Speed against accuracy ("performance" in the settings file, settings_store.h): each
